-----------------------------------------------------

About this fork

Firmware in this repository is distributed as **ultrausbt-Apple-ADB-adapter** (CMake
target `ultrausbt-Apple-ADB-adapter-firmware`). It is a fork of the prior
HIDHopper ADB–based firmware and hardware lineage, continued for the
ultrausbt DIY adapter with Bluetooth, host mode, and related features
for classic ADB Macintosh systems and the Apple IIgs.

-----------------------------------------------------

HIDHopper ADB is a rebranding of the ADBuino and QuokkADB code for Tech
by Androda, LLC. That fork changes the hardware and adds product-specific
tweaks. See: https://github.com/TechByAndroda/HIDHopper_ADB

-----------------------------------------------------

QuokkADB is a re-branding of the adbuino code for Rabbit Hole Computing,
LLC and adds support for the RP2040 microcontroller.
    https://github.com/rabbitholecomputing/QuokkADB-firmware

The primary adbuino tree is intended to live at:
    https://github.com/akuker/adbuino

Original ADBuino / PS/2 work by Rob Braun:
    http://synack.net/~bbraun/   and   http://synack.net/svn/adbduino/
Difegue made additional updates for PS/2:
    https://tvc-16.science/adbuino-ps2.html
    https://github.com/Difegue/Chaotic-Realm
USB Host port originally done by Tony Kuker:
    https://github.com/akuker/adbuino

-----------------------------------------------------

The ADB code is mostly derived from: https://github.com/tmk/tmk_keyboard
(https://github.com/tmk/tmk_keyboard/blob/master/tmk_core/protocol/adb.c)
It was originally ADB host, and was adapted for device use by bbraun.
Below is the license and credit for the original ADB host implementation.

